+For `single` topology with `services.memoryMiB` set to 2048, the services
+workload uses a 256M MySQL buffer pool and 64 connections. Join, sort and read
+buffers are 1M, 2M and 1M; temporary and heap tables are limited to 16M each.
+The API uses one worker with one to four threads. The nested WebUI's dynamic
+PHP pool has at most four children, starts one and keeps one to two spare.
+Only the base and DNS-record Prometheus export timers are disabled; their
+service definitions and the essential scheduler, supervisor and maintenance
+tasks remain available. Other topologies and the normal 4096 MiB configuration
+retain their inherited workload settings. These limits reduce the dedicated
+fixture's concurrency and SQL workspace; excess work may queue or spill to disk.
+They are qualification targets, not a total memory bound or a sustained-fit
+guarantee. They create a distinct guest artifact and do not alter retained
+artifacts through resume.
+
 Include disposable `test-admin` (level 99), `test-user1` and `test-user2`
 (both level 1) accounts from the initial start. Give each a full name, a password
